{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-14T06:21:45.133Z","author":"codex-toolchain-1114b","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"codex","agent_model":"gpt-6.1-sol","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"118a9002071e231c67817b09","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"gpt-6.1-sol","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"high","source":"probe"},"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/2","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-14T06:21:45.133Z","author":"codex-toolchain-1114b","text":"| Failure | Cause (changelog) | Fix |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| coverage branches 99.94 percent; index.ts alias fallback | pm-cli 2026.11.8 GH-1665 maps max-events to maxEvents; named failure is a deliberate coverage fixture | delete unreachable kebab-key fallback; retain typed handler guards; prove spelling-conflict host code/exit 2 and no boundary/output writes |\n\nFocused reporting-window file passes 40/40. Typecheck, lint, duplication, docstrings, canonical-reader acceptance, production audit, pack dry-run, release date, publish attestation and changelog checks pass. Both npm run release:check and bun run release:check complete 363 tests: 361 pass, two fail, zero skipped/canceled. The only failures are the two packed matrices reaching the unchanged 290-second outer deadline (null status), the class already tracked by pm-slack-standup-packed-timing. In both diagnostic reports the touched index.ts is 100 percent in all four dimensions; global diagnostic coverage is statements/lines 96.21, branches 99.88, functions 97.63 because accept-packed.ts is incomplete. Full unchanged coverage and packed certification remain required in CI. Neither deadlines, seed counts, source scope nor thresholds changed. Reverting the removed alias-key branch restores the baseline coverage miss without a behavioral difference; focused tests pass before and after."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-14T06:21:45.133Z"}],"before_h